            "speaker_id": 538335,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good point on speed, but Zone D contains most of our hazardous materials. Given the project's focus on safety, I think we should tackle that one first to mitigate risks early. It's more complex, but it's the highest priority from a safety perspective. Zone F also has some awkwardly shaped heavy machinery that has caused near-misses before.",
